    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1392">

                <pb facs="1739" n="1539" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv02/pg1539"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Mikołajczyk Papers</note>
                <head>No. 1392<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Diary Entry by the Polish Deputy Prime
                        Minister</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Mikołajczyk</hi>)<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d1392-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Babelsberg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-30">July 30, 1945</date>.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>A Polish-American conference was held at the headquarters of the Polish
                        Delegation<anchor n="2" xml:id="d1392-f2"/> concerning a transaction with
                    regard to 2,500 tons of coal to be delivered to the American occupation sector
                    in Berlin. The transaction was based on a payment in dollars, but the Polish
                    side retained the right to accept oil or gasoline in payment for the supply of
                    coal. The Americans would provide railroad freight cars for the coal and would
                    send them to the place of loading.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1392-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d1392-f1-content">
                <p>Cf. <hi rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg480">p. 480</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1392-f2" n="2" xml:id="d1392-f2-content">
                <p>At 10 Domgasse, Babelsberg. See Lane, <hi rendition="#italic">I Saw Poland
                        Betrayed</hi>, p. 130.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
